File: force-app/main/default/classes/RecordAccessService.cls
```apex
public with sharing class RecordAccessService {

    /**
     * Returns the subset of the given record IDs for which the running user has
     * edit access, as reported by the UserRecordAccess virtual object.
     *
     * @param recordIds  Up to 2,000 record IDs (may span multiple objects).
     * @return           A set of IDs that the current user can edit.
     *                   Never returns null; returns an empty set for null/empty input.
     */
    public static Set<Id> editableIds(Set<Id> recordIds) {
        if (recordIds == null || recordIds.isEmpty()) {
            return new Set<Id>();
        }

        Set<Id> editable = new Set<Id>();

        for (UserRecordAccess ura : [
            SELECT RecordId
            FROM UserRecordAccess
            WHERE RecordId IN :recordIds
              AND HasEditAccess = true
        ]) {
            editable.add(ura.RecordId);
        }

        return editable;
    }
}
```

**Why this works:**

| Requirement | How it's met |
|---|---|
| Respects object permissions, ownership, sharing, role hierarchy, View/Modify All | `UserRecordAccess` is the authoritative virtual object that aggregates all of those factors into `HasEditAccess` for the running user. |
| `with sharing` class | Ensures any future queries added to this class respect sharing; the `UserRecordAccess` query itself is a system query that inherently reflects the current user's access. |
| Null / empty input → empty set | Guard clause at the top. |
| IDs may span multiple objects | `RecordId IN :recordIds` is object-agnostic—it matches on the 18-char ID string regardless of the SObject type. |
| ≤ 20 SOQL queries for 2,000 IDs | Exactly **1** SOQL query, regardless of input size (up to the governor limit on `IN` clause size, which is well above 2,000). |
| Bulk-safe | Single query, single pass over results, O(n) set insertion. |

